WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.280
There are countless stories of duos who met&nbsp;
on the set and became off-screen friends.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.480
But in other cases, the lines between reality&nbsp;
and fiction — and between two people — became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.813
starkly different. Here are the TV friends&nbsp;
who couldn't stand each other in real life.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.520
The landmark sitcom from the 1950s, "I Love&nbsp;
Lucy" starred Lucille Ball and Vivian Vance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:26.160
as best friends and co-conspirators&nbsp;
Lucy and Ethel, respectively. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.240
the two actors had a fair amount of animosity&nbsp;
between them, even though they were supposed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.200
play besties on the show. This tension started&nbsp;
the moment that Vance walked onto the set.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.280
There was an unspoken rule in "old-school"&nbsp;
television that no one should compete with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.840
the leading lady in terms of looks. Ethel's&nbsp;
character was supposed to be slightly older,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.320
with a more middle-aged vibe, and Ball&nbsp;
was devastated to see that Vance was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.200
young and attractive instead. So much&nbsp;
so that she wanted the new girl fired.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.920
Over time, however, Vance really began to embody&nbsp;
her character, and her acting skill won Ball&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.880
over professionally — just as her friendship&nbsp;
eventually won her over in real life. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.920
rivalry ended up turning into an actual bond, but&nbsp;
their relationship was quite rocky at the start.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:14.800
On the 1998 supernatural drama "Charmed," Phoebe&nbsp;
and Paige were played by Alyssa Milano and Rose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.520
McGowan. Unfortunately, the two had a toxic&nbsp;
relationship, as McGowan later revealed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.960
a Twitter feud in 2020. She accused Milano&nbsp;
of creating a hostile environment on set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.680
behavior that McGowan called "appalling".&nbsp;
McGowan even went so far as to say that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:35.120
cried every time the show got renewed because of&nbsp;
how difficult her experience was with her co-star.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.600
On the show, Paige and Phoebe have their fair&nbsp;
share of differences, but at the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.080
they save each other's lives and have each&nbsp;
other's backs as true friends and sisters would.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:48.400
But on Twitter, the pair really laid into&nbsp;
each other. What started as a dispute about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.720
politics escalated into McGowan taking&nbsp;
on Milano for everything, from being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:58.160
a fraud and co-opting McGowan's "Cultural&nbsp;
Reset" movement to her salary on "Charmed."

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:03.360
Allegedly, despite what McGowan saw as a high&nbsp;
salary, Milano threw a fit on set, saying that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:08.160
she wasn't paid enough to, quote, “do this s---!"&nbsp;
And McGowan's opposition to Milano's behavior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.400
is just one of a few tense relationships&nbsp;
that Milano was involved in on the show.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.160
“Why does she always pick on me first?”

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.520
In 1995, the fifth series in the "Star&nbsp;
Trek" franchise hit American TVs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.000
becoming a success for seven seasons, and a&nbsp;
landmark show in the realm of gender-balanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.560
casting and the representation of strong&nbsp;
female characters. Two of those characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.800
ended up becoming extremely close on&nbsp;
"Star Trek: Voyager" — Seven of Nine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.600
played by Jeri Ryan, and Captain Kathryn&nbsp;
Janeway, portrayed by Kate Mulgrew.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.880
Seven of Nine arrived on the scene&nbsp;
as a foil to Captain Janeway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.960
much as Spock was to Captain Kirk in&nbsp;
the original series. From the beginning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:49.360
their relationship was meant to be a close one in&nbsp;
which the two characters played off each other.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.800
As the series progressed, the two&nbsp;
became confidantes and friends.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.360
In real life, however, the tensions that arose&nbsp;
from the arrival of newcomer Ryan in Season 4&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.920
incited a tumultuous relationship between&nbsp;
the two stars. With the addition of Ryan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.360
the ratings went through the roof,&nbsp;
painfully leaving Mulgrew in the dust,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.640
according to executive producer Rick&nbsp;
Berman. Speaking with "Woman's World",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.040
he recalled someone from the press literally&nbsp;
pushing past Mulgrew to get to Ryan.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.000
It hurt, and it resulted in an antagonism&nbsp;
that persisted through the end of the show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.720
For one example, Seven's notorious skintight&nbsp;
costume was an element that drew attention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.480
from Janeway in favor of the newcomer. Allegedly,&nbsp;
Mulgrew even tried to prohibit Ryan from going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:33.680
the bathroom during work hours, saying it took&nbsp;
her too long to get out of the costume. Yikes.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.160
In the original "Star Trek" series,&nbsp;
William Shatner, known as Captain Kirk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.840
apparently had some significant beef with Leonard&nbsp;
Nimoy, who played Kirk’s foil and first officer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:49.040
Spock. The beef was allegedly because Nimoy got&nbsp;
more fan letters, despite his intended status&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.000
as a secondary character to Kirk. The Enterprise&nbsp;
captain was supposed to be the obvious protagonist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.520
and fan favorite, but audiences developed a keen&nbsp;
affinity for the pointy-eared science officer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.280
Much of this claim comes from&nbsp;
George Takei, who played Sulu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:08.640
and had an even bigger beef with Shatner...&nbsp;
who also says this fan mail story is made-up.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:13.200
But even if the conflict over fan letters&nbsp;
wasn't part of it, Nimoy and Shatner started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.360
off on tense terms. They clashed often in&nbsp;
the beginning of their professional career&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.920
in part because Nimoy was so singularly&nbsp;
focused on making the most of his moment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:25.680
Though Shatner went on to describe&nbsp;
Nimoy as perhaps his only true friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.880
this relationship ended shortly before Nimoy&nbsp;
passed away. The man who played Spock suddenly cut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:36.160
Shatner out of his life without explanation, and&nbsp;
he died before he or Shatner could make amends.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:41.520
Things aren't always as golden as they may seem,&nbsp;
and all of the characters on "Golden Girls"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:46.720
weren't as chummy in real life as they may have&nbsp;
appeared on TV. This was particularly true of Bea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:52.640
Arthur and Betty White, who portrayed Dorothy and&nbsp;
Rose, respectively. It was a distaste primarily on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:57.120
Arthur's part that stemmed from her views on&nbsp;
White's work ethic. Apparently, she loved to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.360
chat with the audience between scenes instead&nbsp;
of staying focused, as well as her attitude.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.240
The actress who played the cynical Dorothy was&nbsp;
a bit cynical of White's persona in real life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.160
According to those who've worked with&nbsp;
her, White is a pleasant, sunshine-y soul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.560
and that made her pretty popular. Arthur, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:18.320
was convinced that her upbeat attitude was all&nbsp;
an act. White recalled in an HLN interview,

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:21.200
"Sometimes if I was happy, she'd be furious."

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:26.880
“I don’t know what I ever did, but&nbsp;
she was not that thrilled with me.”

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.920
While Arthur apparently wouldn't&nbsp;
give Betty the time of day, White,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:35.040
true to her established image, has mostly kind&nbsp;
words to say about her former co-star. She shared,

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.720
"You didn't mess with Bea! [...] Bea&nbsp;
was very strong. But you loved her."

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.880
Even, apparently, if she didn't love you.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.640
In "Anger Management," Charlie Sheen and Selma&nbsp;
Blair played great friends, occasionally with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:52.080
benefits, Charlie Goodson and Dr. Kate Wales.&nbsp;
But off-screen, it was quite a different story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:56.560
Their tense relationship ended with Blair&nbsp;
getting fired from the show via text message.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:00.640
Leading up to the unceremonious&nbsp;
ousting was quite a lot of anger.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:04.800
It started when Blair voiced concerns to&nbsp;
series executives about Sheen's work ethic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:09.120
The notoriously volatile star was quite unhappy&nbsp;
to see these remarks leaked to the press,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:14.320
giving a decisive ultimatum to the producers.&nbsp;
They had to choose between him and Blair.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.800
Of course, as an executive&nbsp;
producer and star of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.520
it was obvious that Sheen wasn't going to get cut.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.800
“You can’t fire me.”

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.200
Blair was supposed to have a pretty significant&nbsp;
role on the show too, but obviously nothing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:30.240
could compete with Sheen's role or his anger.&nbsp;
Not only did he tell her via text that her days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.800
on "Anger Management" were over, he sprinkled&nbsp;
in a few tasteless four-letter words to boot.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.920
Grace and Karen are close friends on "Will&nbsp;
and Grace," but the actors who portray them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.680
Debra Messing and Megan Mullally,&nbsp;
were apparently anything but.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:48.320
While the last few episodes were filming&nbsp;
in 2019, Mullally missed two episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:53.920
reportedly due to on-set tension. Mullally later&nbsp;
opened up on her husband Nick Offerman's podcast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:58.400
about the fact that she was being "bullied"&nbsp;
at work. Were the two incidents connected?

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:03.040
Well, the description of the situation aligns&nbsp;
with the alleged feud between herself and Messing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:06.960
It’s one involving a situation at work in&nbsp;
which she stood up for herself and made things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.440
quote, "a thousand times worse." She also&nbsp;
noted that it was an ongoing and current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:16.720
situation in January 2020, and "Will &amp; Grace"&nbsp;
was her only regular engagement at that time.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.520
Mullally also ditched a cast interview with&nbsp;
Messing in 2020, ahead of the series finale.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.400
Her leave of absence from the&nbsp;
show suspiciously coincided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:27.920
with her unfollowing both Messing&nbsp;
and fellow "Will and Grace" actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:33.200
Sean Hayes on social media. The latter Mullally&nbsp;
has always publicly gotten along well with.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.880
On Offerman's podcast, she hinted at&nbsp;
the drama behind this choice and her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:39.680
minimal interaction with the cast. She revealed,

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.440
"I'm pretty much on my own."

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:46.080
She added that the alleged bully had recruited&nbsp;
many of her former allies to their side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.640
leaving Mullally without the support she once had.

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.880
Like the on-again, off-again&nbsp;
friends they portrayed on "Glee,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:56.400
Naya Rivera and Lea Michele had&nbsp;
a bit of a rocky relationship.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:01.680
Rivera played Cheerios cheerleading captain&nbsp;
and Glee Club member Santana Lopez, while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:06.320
Michele appeared in the role of the ambitious&nbsp;
and talented Glee Club captain Rachel Berry.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:11.040
On the show, Rachel and Santana began as&nbsp;
bitter rivals. But over multiple periods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:16.160
of tension and reconciliation, they developed&nbsp;
a reputation for their on-and-off friendship.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:20.320
The two live together in New York City and&nbsp;
demonstrate genuine care for one another.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:25.120
Things couldn't have been further from the&nbsp;
truth in real life. In 2014, a fight on the set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:30.000
resulted in one of them getting thrown off set&nbsp;
or storming out, according to varying reports.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.240
Either way, Rivera's character ended up being&nbsp;
written out of the "Glee" finale. Later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:39.040
she revealed that their relationship got so bad&nbsp;
that they didn't speak for the whole of Season 6.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:44.160
Their personalities, she said, were, quote, "not&nbsp;
a good mixture." However, after Rivera's tragic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:48.320
death, Michele paid tribute to her co-star&nbsp;
by posting a photo of her to Instagram,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:52.400
alongside a pic of her late partner and&nbsp;
fellow "Glee" co-star Cory Monteith.

00:08:53.276 --> 00:08:58.720
The names "Mulder and Scully" are synonymous with&nbsp;
the idea of an iconic duo. However, by the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:04.000
"The X-Files" finished airing, Gillian Anderson&nbsp;
and David Duchovny reportedly couldn't stand the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:08.080
sight of each other. While Duchovny initially&nbsp;
had positive things to say about his co-star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:13.120
the relationship deteriorated over the course of&nbsp;
a series of public comments by the two actors.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:18.000
At one point, Duchovny admitted that not only&nbsp;
did he and Anderson not socialize regularly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:22.320
but sometimes the attitude on set&nbsp;
amounted to be pretty bad. As he put it,

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.400
"I'd rather be anywhere else but here,&nbsp;
and I'm going to make you suffer for it!"

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:31.040
That's a pretty dismal revelation, and it&nbsp;
wasn't the only one. After the show ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:35.440
Duchovny confirmed to Metro that the two were&nbsp;
sick of each other by the time the series ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.160
saying, quote, "Familiarity breeds contempt."

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.160
The two actors had an undeniable spark&nbsp;
from the start, but sometimes a spark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:46.480
can turn into a difficult-to-control&nbsp;
fire. Anderson described long periods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:50.480
of their intense relationship in which the&nbsp;
two refused to speak to each other. Often,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:54.240
when they were speaking, Duchovny revealed,&nbsp;
the two would just argue about nothing.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:59.520
Detective Kate Beckett, played by Stana&nbsp;
Katic, and mystery novelist Richard Castle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:05.040
played by Nathan Fillion, were great friends and&nbsp;
star-crossed lovers on ABC's "Castle." However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.000
in real life, the conflict between them grew&nbsp;
so tense that eventually Katic left the show.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:14.320
It must've been a nightmare to work so closely&nbsp;
together while harboring such animosity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:19.040
particularly for Stana Katic. Allegedly, she&nbsp;
would go into her dressing room and cry when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:23.360
filming was done because of nastiness from&nbsp;
Fillion. For multiple seasons leading up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:27.680
Katic's departure and the show's subsequent&nbsp;
cancelation, the actors reportedly despised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:31.200
each other. They also didn't speak&nbsp;
to each other outside of filming.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:35.040
According to “Us Weekly,” the actors actually&nbsp;
had to go to couples counseling together at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:40.080
the behest of the show. This was despite the fact&nbsp;
that they were the furthest thing from a couple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:43.600
unlike their characters. Apparently,&nbsp;
though, it wasn't enough to save Katic's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:47.760
spot on the series. She was subjected to&nbsp;
a harsh exit without, according to her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.800
any insight into the thought&nbsp;
process behind her expulsion.

